# TypeScript testing

- Use the Node.js test runner with `describe` and `it` from `node:test`.
- Use chai `expect` for assertions.
- `yarn test`, `yarn test:unit`, `yarn test:integration`, and `yarn test:e2e` run that suite when it exists. Those commands do not accept extra arguments.
- Run one file or a name pattern with `tsx` and the Node test runner, for example `tsx --test test/unit/services/user-service.test.ts`.
- Mock HTTP with `nock`.
- Build test data with `fishery.Factory`.
